* own model: Texas Instruments TPD4E05U06 (ring U9 and case U6), built only from the maker's datasheet (design/datasheets/codes_tpd4e05u06.pdf; page numbers of the text copy src/codes_tpd4e05u06.txt lines are given).
* Four channels, each a steering-diode pair to GND: clamps at VBR 6.5 V min / 8.5 V max at 1 mA (table at line 546), reverse stand-off VRWM 5.5 V at 10 uA (line 541), leakage 10 nA max and 0.01 nA typ at VIO = 2.5 V (line 564), line capacitance 0.42 to 0.5 pF typ (line 21), dynamic resistance 0.8 ohm (line 580).
* ports: D1P D1N D2P D2N GND(node 0)
* params: rleak  leakage resistance of one channel: 2.5 V / 10 nA = 250 Mohm is the datasheet maximum (default); 2.5 V / 0.01 nA = 250 Gohm is typical
*         vbr    breakdown voltage, default 6.5 V (minimum)
.subckt TPD4E05U06 d1p d1n d2p d2n gnd params: rleak=250Meg vbr=6.5 cio=0.5p
.model Dclamp D(IS=1e-15 N=1 RS=0.8 BV={vbr} IBV=1m CJO=0)
Dp1 0 d1p Dclamp
Dp2 0 d1n Dclamp
Dp3 0 d2p Dclamp
Dp4 0 d2n Dclamp
Rl1 d1p 0 {rleak}
Rl2 d1n 0 {rleak}
Rl3 d2p 0 {rleak}
Rl4 d2n 0 {rleak}
C1 d1p 0 {cio}
C2 d1n 0 {cio}
C3 d2p 0 {cio}
C4 d2n 0 {cio}
.ends TPD4E05U06
